String Handling Functions:
--------------------------
	A String Handling Function is a function used to perform operations on a string

1.  upper() -> 	Converts all characters in a string to uppercase letters.

2.  lower() -> Converts all characters in a string to lowercase letters.

3.  title() -> Converts the first letter of every word into uppercase.
   
4.  strip() -> Removes spaces from the beginning and end of the string.
   
5.  lstrip() ->  Removes spaces only from the left side of the string.
    
6.  rstrip() -> Removes spaces only from the right side of the string.
   
7.  replace() -> Replaces a word or character with another value. 
    
8.  split() -> Splits a string into multiple parts and returns a list.
    
9.  capitalize() -> Converts the first letter of the string to uppercase.
    
10. swapcase() -> Converts uppercase letters to lowercase and lowercase
    letters to uppercase. 

11. join() -> Combines list elements into a single string using a
    separator. 

